W("Case: Kabir's parents list his daily duties and keep reminding him. He feels suffocated and tells his grandmother. What advice might she give, drawing on the poem?", 4, "That children need space and trust as well as rules. Parents should explain their concerns without nagging, and Kabir should speak openly instead of retreating into daydreams. (2+2)", "H"),
