 ("p", "The poem's structure is the interplay of two voices. The adult's voice is brisk and repetitive; its lines are short and blunt. Amanda's brackets are calm and rhymed. By arranging them so, the poet lets us hear a nagging adult and a dreaming child at the same time. The tone is humorous but warm: the poet sides gently with Amanda."),
