 ("p", "*'Don't bite your nails, Amanda! / Don't hunch your shoulders, Amanda!'* These opening commands set the tone: a stream of corrections about small habits. The negative imperatives, and the repeated name, make the adult sound irritable and relentless."),
 ("h3", "Extract 2"),
 ("p", "*'The silence is golden, the freedom is sweet.'* In the orphan daydream Amanda imagines a free life where nobody gives orders. 'Golden' and 'sweet' show how precious silence and freedom seem to her."),
 ("h3", "Extract 3"),
